Message-ID: <4CB852BC.4000303@embl.de>

Hello Walton,

EBImage works fine on Mac systems. It seems that you're facing a problem 
caused by the concurrent installation of different versions of R and/or 
of different architecture (32-bit and 64-bit), unrelated to EBImage.

 From your R CMD INSTALL output, it appears that you installed the 
64-bit version of EBImage, see:
"installing to 
/Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Resources/library/EBImage/libs/x86_64"

What is your version of R, when started from the command line ? Did you 
try to start R and load EBImage from the command line ? Did it work ? 
Did you try to start R64.app and load EBImage ?

The warning message 'Xlib: extension "RANDR" missing on display ":0.0"' 
is caused by the MacPort version of GTK+. I don't know why it pops up 
but it seems harmless.

Hope this helps,

Greg
---
Gregoire Pau
EMBL Research officer
http://www.embl.de/~gpau/

