Message-ID: <8D183C52-4DCA-441C-9F67-EF61B488F39B@uni.no>

Hi Walton,

you are using MacPorts, right? Possibly you unintentionally installed another R as a dependency through MacPorts. I had the same effect. That MacPorts R will be 
$ which R
/opt/local/bin/R
and will become your default R on the console  (if you just type 'R') then, but the packages you install through the GUI don't go there, the  package installs are distinct. The cran Mac R is
normally in  /usr/bin/R
try to find our where the package is installed.

Hope that helps
 Michael

Am Oct 15, 2010 um 3:10 PM schrieb Gregoire Pau:

> Hello Walton,
> 
> EBImage works fine on Mac systems. It seems that you're facing a problem caused by the concurrent installation of different versions of R and/or of different architecture (32-bit and 64-bit), unrelated to EBImage.
> 
> From your R CMD INSTALL output, it appears that you installed the 64-bit version of EBImage, see:
> "installing to /Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Resources/library/EBImage/libs/x86_64"
> 
> What is your version of R, when started from the command line ? Did you try to start R and load EBImage from the command line ? Did it work ? Did you try to start R64.app and load EBImage ?
> 
> The warning message 'Xlib: extension "RANDR" missing on display ":0.0"' is caused by the MacPort version of GTK+. I don't know why it pops up but it seems harmless.
> 
> Hope this helps,
> 
> Greg
